<Base title="About the Calculator & Editorial Approach" description="Learn how this AC to DC calculator separates rectifier models, documents assumptions, cites manufacturer references, and handles corrections."><div class="shell page-intro legal"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} /><span class="eyebrow">CLARITY BEFORE THE CALCULATION</span><h1>A number needs a model.</h1><div class="prose"><p>This site helps explain the output of a single-phase rectifier. Its three models distinguish a capacitor-filtered bridge estimate from ideal unfiltered half-wave and full-wave averages.</p><h2>How results are calculated</h2><p>Formulas, units, examples, assumptions, and technical references appear on the <a href="/ac-to-dc-calculator/#formula">calculator page</a>. The code runs in your browser. Filtered results are simplified estimates and should be interpreted within the stated scope.</p><h2>Our editorial approach</h2><p>Guides link to manufacturer references and distinguish analytical derivations from approximations. The editorial byline describes site content authorship; it does not imply professional certification or independent expert review.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>If a result looks wrong, record all inputs, the selected model, and your expected result with its source. The <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> helps prepare a reproducible report.</p></div></div></Base>
